THIRD-PARTY NOTICES
===================

`@compstats/core` is released under the MIT License; see LICENSE. The package
has no runtime dependency on any third-party code, and no third-party source
file is copied into it.

It does, however, reimplement numerical algorithms whose authorship lies
elsewhere. The package's stated purpose is to return the same doubles R
returns, and reaching that goal meant following published algorithms and, in
several places, the arrangement R gives them: the order of a loop, where a
series is cut off, which branch a value takes. This file records where that
work came from. It is offered as attribution, and it is not a claim that the
parties below endorse this package.

Every routine named here was written in TypeScript for this package. Values
were verified against R, which is a separate program invoked to produce
reference numbers; R itself is not distributed with this package and is not
linked, bundled, or called at runtime.


