2. Applied Statistics algorithms (Royal Statistical Society)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

Several routines implement algorithms published in the Journal of the Royal
Statistical Society, Series C (Applied Statistics). The Royal Statistical
Society holds the copyright in the published routines. The customary
StatLib distribution statement is:

    The Royal Statistical Society holds the copyright to these routines, but
    has given permission for their distribution provided that no fee is
    charged.

The implementations in this package were written in TypeScript from the
published descriptions of the methods; no Fortran or C listing is
redistributed here.

  AS 91    Best, D. J. and Roberts, D. E. (1975). The percentage points of
           the chi-squared distribution. Applied Statistics 24(3), 385-388.
           Used for the starting value in src/core/chisq.ts (`qchisq`).

  AS 109   Cran, G. W., Martin, K. J. and Thomas, G. E. (1977). Inverse of
           the incomplete beta function ratio. Applied Statistics 26(1),
           111-114. The starting value in src/core/special.ts follows the
           same approximation.

  AS 241   Wichura, M. J. (1988). The percentage points of the normal
           distribution. Applied Statistics 37(3), 477-484. The three
           rational regions of `qnorm` in src/core/norm.ts.

  AS 243   Lenth, R. V. (1989). Cumulative distribution function of the
           non-central t distribution. Applied Statistics 38(1), 185-189.
           The series in src/core/tdist.ts.

  AS 275   Ding, C. G. (1992). Computing the non-central chi-squared
           distribution function. Applied Statistics 41(2), 478-482. The
           series used at high noncentrality in src/core/chisq.ts.


