4. Other published methods
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

These are standard results from the literature, implemented from their
published descriptions.

  Lanczos, C. (1964). A precision approximation of the gamma function.
  The log-gamma function in src/core/special.ts.

  Abramowitz, M. and Stegun, I. A. (1964). Handbook of Mathematical
  Functions. Formula 26.2.22 (a normal quantile approximation) in
  src/core/special.ts, and 26.7.10 in src/core/tdist.ts.

  Dekker, T. J. (1971). A floating-point technique for extending the
  available precision. The `twoProduct` and `twoSum` pair that gives
  src/core/arith.ts its software fused multiply-add.

  Sturges, H. A. (1926). The choice of a class interval. The default bin
  count in src/core/histogram.ts.

  Silverman, B. W. (1986). Density Estimation for Statistics and Data
  Analysis. The bandwidth rule in src/core/kde.ts.

  Jacobi rotations for the symmetric eigenproblem, in
  src/core/linalg/eigen.ts.

  Nash, J. C. (1990). Compact Numerical Methods for Computers. R's `optim`
  implements Nash's algorithm 21. The BFGS routine in src/core/optim.ts
  reaches the same optima but does not follow Nash's line search; its
  differences from R are stated at the function.


